     "up": {"title":"Name the evaluation criterion (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Harder comments: none of them names its criterion. Match each criterion to the comment from a Caribbean problem-solver that judges an option against it.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Effectiveness","r":"Barcoded wristbands would cut the Belize City clinic's file search from 70 minutes to under five, closing almost the whole gap"},{"l":"Cost","r":"Over five years, the subscription fees add up to more than buying the licensed package outright"},{"l":"Time","r":"The new kiosks cannot reach Antigua before the cricket season ends, and the queues disappear after that anyway"},{"l":"Feasibility","r":"The Grenada cooperative's warehouse has no reliable Internet, so a cloud-only system could not run there"},{"l":"Impact and risks","r":"Collecting members' ID numbers on a free online form could expose them if the form provider is hacked"},{"l":"Sustainability","r":"The volunteer who would build the spreadsheet leaves for university in August, and no one else can maintain it"}],"win":"Excellent. You recognised each criterion from its meaning: total cost over time, a deadline that makes a solution pointless, missing equipment, a data risk, and maintenance that keeps a solution working."}
