     "up": {"title":"Match the problem-solving term (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>A health clinic in Belize City cannot find patients' files quickly. Match each term to the example from the clinic's problem-solving.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Symptom","r":"Patients complain loudly in the waiting room"},{"l":"Current state","r":"Finding a patient's file takes an average of 25 minutes"},{"l":"Desired state","r":"Any patient's file is found within two minutes of arrival"},{"l":"Root cause","r":"Files are filed by first name in some drawers and by surname in others"},{"l":"Requirement","r":"Any nurse must be able to find a file without help from the records clerk"},{"l":"Constraint","r":"The clinic has no budget for new computers this year"},{"l":"Optimal solution","r":"One agreed surname-first rule with colour-coded labels: the best fit to the needs and the zero budget"},{"l":"Feedback","r":"The review shows night-shift nurses still misfile, so the team returns to analysis"}],"win":"Well matched. Using these eight terms precisely, and keeping requirement and constraint apart, is what \"describe\" and \"explain\" questions reward."}
