     "up": {"title":"Stage quick-fire (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Jolly Harbour Ferry in Antigua sells tickets from a paper book. Boats leave half-empty while customers are told they are full. Name the stage for each action. Some actions are designed to mislead.</p>","items":[{"text":"The manager finds that the ticket book is updated only when the clerk returns from lunch, so seats sold at the pier are never recorded.","options":["implement","evaluate and review","define the problem","analyse the problem"],"answer":3,"fb":"Finding why the gap exists is analysis."},{"text":"The team agrees with the owner that the problem is \"boats leave with an average of 18 empty seats while customers are turned away\", not \"we need an app\".","options":["analyse the problem","define the problem","select and justify the optimal solution","identify possible solutions"],"answer":1,"fb":"Agreeing a solution-neutral statement of the problem is definition."},{"text":"The team lists that any solution must work without Internet at the pier and cost less than EC$5,000.","options":["select and justify the optimal solution","analyse the problem","implement","define the problem"],"answer":1,"fb":"Requirements and constraints are identified during analysis."},{"text":"The team judges a tablet booking system: it would record sales instantly, but the pier has weak mobile signal.","options":["implement","evaluate and review","define the problem","identify and evaluate possible solutions"],"answer":3,"fb":"Judging an option's strength and weakness BEFORE any choice is stage 3, not stage 6."},{"text":"The team recommends the tablet system with an offline mode, explaining why it beats an extra clerk on cost and an online-only system on reliability.","options":["select and justify the optimal solution","evaluate and review","identify and evaluate possible solutions","analyse the problem"],"answer":0,"fb":"A choice with reasons that compare it with each alternative is select and justify."},{"text":"The team tries the tablet system on the Saturday boat only, with the paper book kept as a backup.","options":["evaluate and review","implement","identify and evaluate possible solutions","analyse the problem"],"answer":1,"fb":"A pilot is a careful way of putting the chosen solution into action: implementation."},{"text":"After two months, empty seats have fallen to 6 per trip, but weekend queues at the kiosk are longer.","options":["define the problem","implement","analyse the problem","evaluate and review"],"answer":3,"fb":"Measuring results and spotting a side effect after go-live is evaluation and review."}],"win":"Excellent. You separated stage 3 judgements from stage 6 judgements, recognised requirements as analysis, and saw that a pilot is part of implementation."}
