     "up": {"title":"Define, analyse or evaluate and review? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Now both \"evaluate\" stages are in play. Sort each activity from a hardware store in Mandeville, Jamaica, whose stock records do not match the shelves. Remember: stage 3 judges options BEFORE a choice; stage 6 judges the chosen solution AFTER it is implemented.</p>","bins":["Define the problem","Analyse the problem","Identify and evaluate possible solutions","Evaluate and review"],"items":[{"t":"Agreeing with the owner that the problem is the mismatch between records and shelves, not \"the old till\"","bin":0,"fb":"Agreeing what the problem is, without naming a fix, is part of defining it."},{"t":"Listing that any solution must work during power cuts and cost under J$400,000","bin":1,"fb":"Requirements and constraints are identified in analysis."},{"t":"Counting, three months after go-live, how often the records and the shelves disagree","bin":3,"fb":"Measuring the chosen solution's results is evaluation and review."},{"t":"Stating that customers are told about 15 times a week that items are in stock when they are not, and that builders will go elsewhere if this continues","bin":0,"fb":"Who, how and consequence: the problem definition."},{"t":"Finding at the review that Saturday deliveries are still missed, and returning to analysis","bin":3,"fb":"A review that sends the team back to an earlier stage is evaluation and review."},{"t":"Comparing a barcode stock system with weekly manual stock counts, giving a strength and a weakness of each","bin":2,"fb":"Judging options before any is chosen is stage 3."},{"t":"Asking counter staff whether the low-stock alerts arrive in time to reorder","bin":3,"fb":"Feedback on a solution in use belongs to evaluation and review."},{"t":"Breaking the problem into receiving, selling and returns","bin":1,"fb":"Decomposing the problem is analysis."},{"t":"Judging that the barcode system would be fast but would need staff training, before any decision is made","bin":2,"fb":"This is still a judgement of an option before selection: stage 3."},{"t":"Finding that deliveries collected from the yard are never entered into the stock records","bin":1,"fb":"This identifies a cause: analysis."}],"win":"Well done. Define says what the problem is, analyse explains why and what limits apply, stage 3 judges options before choosing, and evaluate and review judges the chosen solution after it is in use."}
