     "type": "multi",
     "game": true,
     "title": "Closing the gap with information",
     "intro": "<p>Every problem is a gap between a present situation and a goal situation, and information is needed at every stage of closing it. Read each short Caribbean situation and choose the best answer.</p>",
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "Kezia, a Breadfruit Valley Secondary student, has failed her last two CAPE IT Unit 1 tests and wants a Grade II in the final exam. \"She has failed her last two tests\" describes her...",
       "options": [
        "Goal situation",
        "Solution",
        "Present situation",
        "Physical resource"
       ],
       "answer": 2,
       "fb": "Where she is now is the present situation. The Grade II she wants is the goal situation; problem solving closes the gap between them."
      },
      {
       "text": "For the same student, \"a Grade II in the final CAPE IT Unit 1 exam\" describes her...",
       "options": [
        "Present situation",
        "Information resource",
        "Goal situation",
        "Research"
       ],
       "answer": 2,
       "fb": "Where she wants to be is the goal situation."
      },
      {
       "text": "A farmer in Guyana whose bora bean plants are being eaten asks an agricultural officer to identify the insect and count the damaged plants per row. At which stage of problem solving is this information mainly used?",
       "options": [
        "Select and justify the best solution",
        "Implement the solution",
        "Define and analyse the problem",
        "Evaluate and review"
       ],
       "answer": 2,
       "fb": "Identifying the pest and measuring the damage tells the farmer exactly what is wrong and how serious it is: defining and analysing the problem."
      },
      {
       "text": "Three months after moving its shelves to make space for a cold drinks fridge, the Belmopan Minimart compares its new monthly sales with last year's figures. At which stage is this information used?",
       "options": [
        "Define the problem",
        "Evaluate and review",
        "Identify possible solutions",
        "Analyse the problem"
       ],
       "answer": 1,
       "fb": "Checking new figures after the change shows whether the solution worked: evaluate and review."
      },
      {
       "text": "A clinic in Port-au-Prince has enough nurses, beds and medicine, but patients wait for hours because staff cannot see which patients have appointments at which times. What does the clinic mainly lack?",
       "options": [
        "Equipment",
        "Goal situation",
        "Information resources",
        "Physical resources"
       ],
       "answer": 2,
       "fb": "The materials, people and equipment are there. What is missing is knowledge of who is booked when: an information resource."
      },
      {
       "text": "A Noord family reads its electricity bills, sees that usage jumped after their old fridge began to leak, and uses those figures to decide to replace the fridge. Which step of \"understand → inform → solve\" is the decision to replace the fridge?",
       "options": [
        "Understand",
        "Inform",
        "Solve",
        "None of these"
       ],
       "answer": 2,
       "fb": "Using the information to choose a response is the solve step. Reading the bills helped them understand; the figures informed the decision."
      },
      {
       "text": "Before her first evening lecture at Coralstone College, Nadia checks the campus map to find room B12. Which everyday research habit is this?",
       "options": [
        "Find a contact",
        "Find a cure",
        "Find the time",
        "Find a place"
       ],
       "answer": 3,
       "fb": "Locating a room is \"find a place\", one of the simple research habits we use every day."
      }
     ],
     "win": "Well done. You placed the present and goal situations, linked information to the stages of problem solving, told physical resources from information resources and recognised everyday research.",
     "tutor": [
      {
       "h": "Now versus wanted",
       "p": "<p>The present situation is where things stand now. The goal situation is where you want to be. The problem is the gap between them.</p>"
      },
      {
       "h": "Which stage?",
       "p": "<p>Finding out what is wrong = define and analyse. Checking results after the change = evaluate and review.</p>"
      },
      {
       "h": "Things or knowledge?",
       "p": "<p>If the people, materials and equipment are already there but nobody knows who, where or when, the gap is in information resources.</p>"
      }
     ],
