     "up": {"title":"Same information, different problem (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Harder pairings, including cosmetic claims and borderline cases. For each, choose the category the information belongs to FOR THE DECISION NAMED.</p>","items":[{"text":"A ferry's passenger list (names and ID numbers), for the Nevis port authority accounting for everyone on board after an accident at sea.","options":["Extraneous","Desirable","Essential","Cosmetic"],"answer":2,"fb":"Rescuers cannot account for every passenger without the list. Essential."},{"text":"The same passenger list, for the ferry company choosing a new paint colour for its boats.","options":["Desirable","Extraneous","Essential","Cosmetic"],"answer":1,"fb":"Names and ID numbers have no bearing on paint colour. Extraneous for this decision."},{"text":"A rum distillery's statement to Barbados regulators that \"our waste water is perfectly clean\", sent instead of laboratory test results.","options":["Cosmetic","Desirable","Extraneous","Essential"],"answer":0,"fb":"It looks like evidence of safety but masks the missing test results. Cosmetic: the regulators must ask for the data."},{"text":"Laboratory test results for the distillery's waste water, for the same regulators deciding whether to renew its licence.","options":["Cosmetic","Extraneous","Essential","Desirable"],"answer":2,"fb":"The licence decision cannot be made safely without measured results. Essential."},{"text":"Online reviews of a jerk centre in Ocho Rios, for a visitor choosing where to eat tonight.","options":["Extraneous","Essential","Cosmetic","Desirable"],"answer":3,"fb":"Reviews help the choice, but the visitor could still decide without them. Desirable."},{"text":"The jerk centre's opening hours, for the same visitor.","options":["Desirable","Essential","Cosmetic","Extraneous"],"answer":1,"fb":"If the centre is closed tonight, the choice fails. Essential."},{"text":"An estate agent's assurance that \"this street never floods\", given instead of the official flood map, for a Georgetown family deciding whether a house is safe to buy.","options":["Essential","Desirable","Extraneous","Cosmetic"],"answer":3,"fb":"It sounds like flood information but masks the missing map, and the agent gains from the sale. Cosmetic: ask for the map."},{"text":"The colour the house is painted, for the same family judging its flood risk.","options":["Cosmetic","Extraneous","Desirable","Essential"],"answer":1,"fb":"Paint colour has no bearing on flood risk. Extraneous."}],"win":"Excellent. The category belongs to the pair of information and decision. Cosmetic claims stand where real evidence should be, so the right response is always to ask for that evidence."}
