     "up": {"title":"Cosmetic or desirable? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"<p>The board of a credit union in St. George's, Grenada, must decide whether to open a new branch in Grenville. Each item below was placed in the board's briefing pack.</p><p>Which item is BEST described as <b>cosmetic</b> information for this decision?</p>","options":[{"t":"Survey results showing that 38% of Grenville residents would open an account at a local branch","fb":"This is measured evidence about demand that directly informs the decision. It is essential, not cosmetic."},{"t":"A consultant's slide stating that \"Grenville is a booming market with huge potential\", with no population, income or competitor figures","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. It looks like market evidence but masks the missing figures, so it cannot guide the decision. The board should ask for the data behind the claim."},{"t":"A history of how the credit union was founded","fb":"True, but it has no bearing on whether to open in Grenville. Extraneous, not cosmetic."},{"t":"Members' preferred opening hours for the new branch","fb":"Useful for planning the service, but the board can decide whether to open without it. Desirable."}]}
