     "up": {"title":"Run the validity questions (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Harder cases: more than one criterion may seem to fit, so choose the one the evidence points to MOST strongly. Read every detail before you answer.</p>","items":[{"text":"A Trinidad cement company's press release calls its new mix \"the strongest in the region\", quoting only tests run in its own laboratory.","options":["Cultural context","Completeness","Bias","Accuracy","Currency"],"answer":2,"fb":"The company gains from the claim and quotes only its own tests, so the source is not objective. Accuracy is uncertain too, but the motive is the strongest warning sign."},{"text":"A 2025 report on Caribbean tourist arrivals gives figures for Barbados, Jamaica and the Bahamas but none for the Leeward Islands, and a planner in Antigua wants to use it.","options":["Cultural context","Bias","Accuracy","Currency","Completeness"],"answer":4,"fb":"The figures may be correct and recent, but the part the Antiguan planner needs is missing. Completeness fails."},{"text":"A farming leaflet used in Grenada sets planting dates by spring, summer, autumn and winter.","options":["Accuracy","Completeness","Currency","Cultural context","Bias"],"answer":3,"fb":"The leaflet assumes a temperate climate with four seasons. Grenada has wet and dry seasons, so the advice does not fit: cultural context."},{"text":"A table of euro exchange rates against the Eastern Caribbean dollar was correct when a magazine printed it in March. A shopkeeper in St. Kitts uses it to price imported goods in October.","options":["Currency","Completeness","Bias","Cultural context","Accuracy"],"answer":0,"fb":"The rates were right in March, but exchange rates change daily. The information is no longer current enough: currency."},{"text":"A Jamaican blog reports that a school's CSEC pass rate this year was 112%.","options":["Completeness","Bias","Currency","Accuracy","Cultural context"],"answer":3,"fb":"A pass rate above 100% is impossible, so the figure contains an error. Accuracy fails."},{"text":"A survey on whether Roseau residents want a new cruise pier was answered only by members of the tourism association that campaigned for the pier.","options":["Currency","Bias","Completeness","Cultural context","Accuracy"],"answer":1,"fb":"The sample was drawn from people who already favour the pier, so the result is slanted. Selection of the sample is a source of bias."},{"text":"A news site says a storm passed 30 km south of Grenada, while the official advisory and two other news sites all say 130 km.","options":["Completeness","Cultural context","Currency","Accuracy","Bias"],"answer":3,"fb":"Cross-checking with independent sources shows the figure is wrong, probably a typing error. Accuracy fails."}],"win":"Excellent. You looked for the strongest evidence each time: a motive or slanted sample (bias), impossible or conflicting figures (accuracy), a mismatch of place or climate (cultural context), a missing part (completeness) and age (currency)."}
