     "up": {"title":"Match the criterion to the warning sign (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Harder warning signs: some need a quick calculation or a careful read. Match each criterion to the sign that points to it.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Bias","r":"A survey about a new Montego Bay hotel was answered only by people the developer invited"},{"l":"Accuracy","r":"A report says 45% of a town's 72,000 people are under 25, then gives that group as 3,240 people"},{"l":"Completeness","r":"A comparison of three laptops gives their prices but not shipping, import duty or warranty costs"},{"l":"Currency","r":"An undated web page on the Barbados minimum wage quotes rates set several years ago"},{"l":"Cultural context","r":"A sales plan for a Port of Spain store places its biggest sale in Thanksgiving week and ignores Carnival"},{"l":"Un-refereed source","r":"A post claiming a bush tea cures diabetes, shared by a page with no named author and no expert review"}],"win":"Excellent. You spotted a hand-picked sample (bias), a figure that contradicts its own percentage (45% of 72,000 is 32,400), missing costs (completeness), an old undated page (currency), a plan built around another country's holidays (cultural context) and a claim nobody checked (un-refereed)."}
