     "up": {"title":"Decode the URL (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Harder addresses with sections, country codes and personal pages. The addresses below are examples. Read each domain name carefully and decide who is most likely to host the page.</p>","items":[{"t":"library.marineresearch.edu/guides/sargassum","bin":0,"fb":"The domain ends in .edu. \"library\" is just a section of the academic site."},{"t":"www.oceanstudies.ac.jm/staff/publications","bin":0,"fb":".ac before the country code .jm (Jamaica) marks an academic organisation."},{"t":"www.islandsolar.com.tt/get-a-quote","bin":1,"fb":".com before the country code .tt (Trinidad and Tobago) marks a commercial organisation."},{"t":"shop.reefsafe.co.uk/sunscreen","bin":1,"fb":".co before a country code, and a shop section: commercial."},{"t":"www.oceanstudies.ac.jm/~dthomas/my-reef-tips.html","bin":2,"fb":"The host is academic, but the tilde and personal name show a page published by an individual, which the university may not have checked."},{"t":"reeflover-carla.freeblogsite.com/posts/my-dive","bin":2,"fb":"The .com belongs to the free blog service. The personal name in front of it shows a private individual's blog."},{"t":"www.caribbeandivegear.lc/specials","bin":1,"fb":"A business on St. Lucia's country code with a \"specials\" page: commercial."},{"t":"www.freepages-host.net/~marcus/beach-cleanup.html","bin":2,"fb":"A tilde and a first name on a free hosting site: a private individual."},{"t":"www.coastalstudies.edu/news/2026-report","bin":0,"fb":"A news section on a .edu domain: academic."}],"win":"Well decoded. Read the domain name (the part before the first single slash) from the right: a country code shows where, .edu, .ac, .com and .co show what type, and a tilde or a free blog address shows a personal page, even on a university or business server."}
