     "stimulus": "<p class=\"passage\">The Sunset Snacks food truck parks near Palm Beach and Eagle Beach. Sales have fallen over the last three months. The owner, Mr. Croes, wants to decide whether to move to a new location in Oranjestad on cruise ship days. While researching, he has collected: the cruise ship arrival schedule for the Oranjestad cruise port; his daily sales for the past year; the fee for a vending permit in Oranjestad; the number of food stalls already operating near the cruise pier; a list of song lyrics his daughter likes; the history of the food truck industry in the USA; customer comments on his social media page; and a friend's assurance that \"everybody in Oranjestad will buy from you\", although no one has counted the customers there.</p>",
     "prompt": "<p>(a) Identify <b>three</b> items of information that are <b>essential</b> to Mr. Croes's decision, and explain why each is essential. <i>(4 marks)</i></p><p>(b) From the stimulus, give one example each of <b>desirable</b>, <b>extraneous</b> and <b>cosmetic</b> information, briefly justifying each category. <i>(3 marks)</i></p><p>(c) State what type of problem (personal, commercial, scientific or social) this is. <i>(1 mark)</i></p>",
