     "up": {"title":"Order the prototyping cycle (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Bright Smile Dental Clinic's booking system is again being built by evolutionary prototyping, but this time with two rounds of feedback and the move to the final system. Put all eight steps in order.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"Meet the receptionist and dentists to agree the outline requirements: book, cancel and send reminders"},{"t":"Quickly build version 1, starting with the best-understood requirement: booking a slot"},{"t":"Staff and five patients try version 1 and ask for a clearer calendar and a reminder message"},{"t":"Build version 2 with a redesigned calendar and a reminder feature"},{"t":"Users test version 2 and request only small wording changes"},{"t":"Make the final changes, then tidy the code and write the documentation"},{"t":"Fully test the completed system, including the security of patient data"},{"t":"Implement the system at the clinic and train the receptionist"}],"win":"Correct. Outline requirements, then build, evaluate and refine twice, each version starting from users' comments on the last. Only when users are satisfied is the system tidied, fully tested and implemented. That repeated loop is what makes the development evolutionary."}
