     "up": {"title":"Match the scenario clue to the model (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Harder: six clues, including two kinds of prototype and the separate meanings of iterative and incremental. Match each clue to the model or term it points to.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"\"The auditors must approve the design before a line of code is written.\"","r":"Waterfall"},{"l":"\"Staff disagree about the screens, so let them try a rough version that we will discard before the real build.\"","r":"Throwaway prototype"},{"l":"\"Keep improving the version the volunteers are already using until it does everything they need.\"","r":"Evolutionary prototype"},{"l":"\"Applications must open next month; appeals and reports can come in later releases.\"","r":"Incremental development"},{"l":"\"Take the search screen through another full cycle, because users still find it confusing.\"","r":"Iterative development"},{"l":"\"The founder joins our ten-minute meeting every morning and reorders the backlog each fortnight.\"","r":"Agile software development"}],"win":"Correct. Approval before coding (Waterfall), discard versus keep (the two prototypes), later releases (incremental), another full cycle on the same part (iterative), and daily meetings with a reordered backlog (Agile)."}
