      "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> Prototyping builds a working model so that users can try it and give feedback, whereas iterative/incremental development delivers the system in working parts, each adding new functions.</p><p><b>(b)</b> I recommend Agile software development.</p><p><b>(c)</b> Clue 1: The scenario says \"We are not sure what guests want.\" This model helps because Agile welcomes changing requirements, so the hotel can add the features guests actually ask for. Clue 2: The scenario says \"Our front-office manager can meet the developers every week.\" This model helps because she can act as the customer representative who reviews each sprint and sets priorities.</p><p><b>(d)</b> One disadvantage of Agile is that the final cost is hard to predict because the scope keeps changing.</p>",
      "teacherTip": "<p>Dial-down: accept Agile or iterative/incremental in (b), provided the clues in (c) are linked to that model. Once a student scores well here, move them to the full 15-mark version.</p>"
