     "up": {"title":"Which type of feasibility? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Harder findings from a Grenada credit union considering a mobile banking app. Watch for staff expertise, intangible benefits and management support.</p>","items":[{"t":"The credit union's core banking software cannot connect to a mobile app without an upgrade","bin":0,"fb":"Whether existing technology can handle it: technical."},{"t":"The only IT officer has never managed a system that is open to the Internet","bin":0,"fb":"Whether existing staff have the technical expertise is also technical feasibility."},{"t":"The app and upgrade will cost EC$95,000; fewer branch visits should save one teller post, worth EC$40,000 a year","bin":1,"fb":"Costs compared with a tangible benefit: economic."},{"t":"Members are expected to trust the credit union more because they can check their balances at any time","bin":1,"fb":"An intangible benefit still counts in the cost/benefit analysis: economic."},{"t":"Loan approvals would still need a signature at a branch, so the approval procedure stays the same","bin":2,"fb":"Fit with existing procedures: operational."},{"t":"The board fully supports the project and has named a manager to lead it","bin":2,"fb":"Management support is part of operational feasibility."},{"t":"Older members in rural parishes say they distrust phone banking and will keep visiting branches","bin":3,"fb":"Whether users will adapt: social/behavioural."},{"t":"Tellers fear the app will lead to branch closures and job cuts","bin":3,"fb":"Fear of job losses affects acceptance: social/behavioural."},{"t":"The board wants the app live before the Christmas shopping season, five months away","bin":4,"fb":"A deadline the project must meet: time."},{"t":"The vendor can start only when its current project ends in four months, leaving one month to build and test","bin":4,"fb":"Time needed compared with time available: time feasibility."}],"win":"Well sorted. Staff expertise is technical, intangible benefits such as trust still count as economic, management support and procedures are operational, attitudes of members and staff are social/behavioural, and deadlines and schedules are time."}
