     "up": {"title":"What belongs in the system proposal? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>The junior analyst at Seaside Pharmacy has a longer draft list. Several items are good documents, but they belong to later stages of the SDLC.</p>","q":"Tap EVERY line that belongs in the system proposal.","lines":["1. Problem definition: medicines run out unnoticed about twice a month because stock is tracked on paper cards.","2. Objective: cut emergency medicine orders from about eight a month to no more than one within six months.","3. Terms of reference: requested by the owner; covers stock control at the Gros Islet branch only.","4. The database table design for the stock file, with field names and data types.","5. Constraint: the system must run on the existing back-office PC and cost no more than USD 15,000.","6. A test plan with boundary values for reorder levels.","7. Expected benefit: less money lost on expired stock.","8. The dates each programmer will start and finish coding.","9. A conversion plan for entering the paper stock cards.","10. The cashiers' training timetable for go-live week."],"correct":[0,1,2,4,6],"win":"Correct. The proposal holds the problem definition, measurable objectives, terms of reference, constraints and expected benefits. Table designs belong to design, test plans to development, coding dates to the project plan, and conversion plans and training timetables to implementation.","miss":"Look again. Ask of each line: could it be written before anyone has decided to go ahead? If it depends on a design, a schedule or a built system, it belongs to a later stage."}
