     "up": {"title":"What belongs in the conversion plan? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Leeward Credit Union's assistant has produced a longer list of possible contents for the conversion plan. Several are good documents that belong to other stages.</p>","q":"Tap EVERY line that belongs in the conversion plan.","lines":["1. Changeover method: a pilot at the small Little Bay branch for one month, chosen because its manager is experienced.","2. How success will be judged: no unexplained balance differences after the first week.","3. Member balances to be converted by the IT officer and checked by two senior tellers.","4. The project's overall budget and the feasibility study's go decision.","5. The design of the screen tellers use to look up a member.","6. Training: two sessions for each teller, using the user manual, in the week before go-live.","7. Unit test results for the interest module.","8. Fallback: the old system stays ready for one month, with a full backup taken before conversion.","9. Requirement: the system must calculate interest daily.","10. Timetable: install on Friday, convert data on Saturday and Sunday, go live on Monday."],"correct":[0,1,2,5,7,9],"win":"Correct. The conversion plan covers the method and its reason, how success will be judged, data conversion with responsibilities, training, fallback and the timetable. Budgets and go decisions belong to the feasibility stage, screen designs to design, test results to development and requirements to analysis.","miss":"Look again. The conversion plan assumes the system is already built and tested. Its job is to manage the switch."}
