     "up": {"title":"Testing or review? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","q":"<p>Four activities from Statia Port Authority's cargo-tracking project are described below. Each could be mistaken for review. Which one is part of the <b>review</b> stage?</p>","options":[{"t":"Five months after go-live, the team compares lost container records with the target in the system proposal and checks actual running costs against the feasibility estimates","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. Measuring the live system against the proposal's objectives and the original cost estimates is review."},{"t":"Staff are surveyed about how containers are tracked on paper, to find out what the new system must do","fb":"Surveys can appear in several stages, but investigating the current system to set requirements is analysis."},{"t":"In the first week after go-live, the old system stays ready in case the new one fails","fb":"A fallback during changeover belongs to implementation and the conversion plan."},{"t":"Before go-live, port staff use the system for a week and sign to confirm it meets their requirements","fb":"That is acceptance testing, part of development, before go-live."}]}
