      "prompt": "<p>Answer ALL parts. Short answers are fine.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>(i) State what a feasibility study decides. <i>(1 mark)</i><br>(ii) Name the deliverable the feasibility study produces. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>(i) Complete: \"Economic feasibility checks whether ...\" <i>(1 mark)</i><br>(ii) Complete: \"Operational feasibility checks whether ...\" <i>(1 mark)</i><br>(iii) Give ONE example from the scenario of either type. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>Name ONE deliverable for EACH stage: <b>design</b>, <b>development</b>, <b>implementation</b>. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Complete: \"A user manual is written for ..., whereas a technical manual is written for ...\" <i>(2 marks)</i></li></ol>",
