      "stimulus": "<p class=\"passage\">Island Breeze Hotels group has three hotels: Dickenson Bay, St. John's and Barbuda. Its new reservations and billing system is built and tested. Guests' bookings and payments must not be lost, high season starts in two months, and the IT team is small.</p>",
      "prompt": "<p>Answer ALL parts. Short answers are fine.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>(i) Name ONE suitable changeover method for Island Breeze Hotels. <i>(1 mark)</i><br>(ii) Give TWO reasons from the scenario for your choice. <i>(2 marks)</i><br>(iii) State ONE reason why direct changeover would be risky. <i>(1 mark)</i></li><li>List THREE items the conversion plan should include. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Complete: \"The review stage happens ... and checks whether ...\" <i>(2 marks)</i></li><li>State ONE software engineering practice that would reduce the risk of the system failing. <i>(1 mark)</i></li></ol>",
      "min": 80,
