     "up": {"title":"Read the Hilltop Bakery Gantt chart (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Belair Pharmacy in Bridgetown, Barbados, is developing a stock system. Its Gantt chart shows:</p><div class=\"tablewrap\"><table><tr><th>Task</th><th>Weeks</th></tr><tr><td>A Feasibility study</td><td>1 to 2</td></tr><tr><td>B Analysis</td><td>3 to 6</td></tr><tr><td>C Design</td><td>6 to 8</td></tr><tr><td>D Development</td><td>8 to 14</td></tr><tr><td>E Testing</td><td>12 to 15</td></tr><tr><td>F Training</td><td>14 to 15</td></tr><tr><td>G Implementation</td><td>16 to 17</td></tr></table></div>","items":[{"text":"How long does Development last?","options":["7 weeks","6 weeks","14 weeks","8 weeks"],"answer":0,"fb":"14 − 8 + 1 = 7 weeks."},{"text":"In which weeks do Development and Testing overlap?","options":["They do not overlap","Weeks 12 to 15 (4 weeks)","Weeks 12 to 14 (3 weeks)","Weeks 12 and 13 (2 weeks)"],"answer":2,"fb":"Testing starts in week 12 and Development ends in week 14, so weeks 12, 13 and 14 are shared."},{"text":"Which tasks are running in week 14?","options":["D and E only","D, E and F","E and F only","D only"],"answer":1,"fb":"Development (8 to 14), Testing (12 to 15) and Training (14 to 15) all include week 14."},{"text":"What is the total length of the project, and why is it less than the sum of the durations?","options":["24 weeks, because each task must finish before the next","15 weeks, because implementation is not counted","17 weeks, because testing is not counted","17 weeks, because several tasks overlap"],"answer":3,"fb":"Week 1 to week 17 is 17 weeks. The durations add to 24 weeks (2 + 4 + 3 + 7 + 4 + 2 + 2), but overlaps shorten the project."},{"text":"Which two tasks are sequential, with no overlap?","options":["A and B","B and C","C and D","D and E"],"answer":0,"fb":"A ends in week 2 and B starts in week 3. B and C share week 6, C and D share week 8, and D and E share weeks 12 to 14."},{"text":"Development slips and now ends in week 16. Testing must end one week after Development ends, and Implementation (2 weeks) starts the week after Testing ends. In which week does the project now end?","options":["Week 18","Week 19","Week 21","Week 17"],"answer":1,"fb":"Testing now ends in week 17, so Implementation runs in weeks 18 and 19."},{"text":"Which limitation of the Gantt chart does the previous question expose?","options":["A Gantt chart shows too few tasks","The bars do not show which tasks depend on others, so the knock-on effect of a delay must be worked out separately","A Gantt chart cannot show durations","A Gantt chart cannot be updated"],"answer":1,"fb":"The chart shows timing, but not that Testing and Implementation depend on Development finishing."}],"win":"Well analysed. You calculated durations with the +1, found overlaps and concurrent tasks, explained why the project is shorter than the sum of durations, and traced the knock-on effect of a delay, which the bars alone do not show."}
