     "up": {"title":"Choosing the right CASE tool (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Pitons Software in St. Lucia is building a patient-booking system for a clinic in Soufrière. The team must schedule the project, model the data, let nurses try the screens, manage code from four programmers and retest after every fix, all on a small budget.</p>","items":[{"text":"Which category and phase fit \"schedule the project and track its milestones\"?","options":["UI prototyping (e.g. Balsamiq), design","Code and version control (e.g. Git), development","Project management (e.g. Jira), project planning","Testing (e.g. Selenium), testing"],"answer":2,"fb":"Gantt schedules and milestones come from project management tools, in planning."},{"text":"The analysts need an ER diagram of PATIENT, APPOINTMENT and DOCTOR. Which category and phase?","options":["UI prototyping, development","Diagramming and modelling, analysis and design","Project management, review","Testing, testing"],"answer":1,"fb":"ER diagrams are drawn with diagramming and modelling tools in analysis and design."},{"text":"Nurses must try the booking screens before coding. Which category, and which type of CASE?","options":["UI prototyping; lower CASE","Version control; upper CASE","UI prototyping; upper CASE","Testing; lower CASE"],"answer":2,"fb":"Clickable screens for design are UI prototyping, which supports the early phases: upper CASE."},{"text":"Four programmers will edit the same code. What is the MAIN risk without version control?","options":["The ERD cannot be drawn","One programmer's changes overwrite another's, and a broken change cannot easily be rolled back","The prototype cannot be shown","The Gantt chart cannot be updated"],"answer":1,"fb":"Version control records every change and who made it, so work is merged safely and can be rolled back."},{"text":"After every fix, the team wants all earlier tests rerun automatically. Which category, and what is this kind of testing called?","options":["Version control; unit testing","Testing tools; regression testing","Testing tools; acceptance testing","Project management; integration testing"],"answer":1,"fb":"Re-running earlier tests after a change is regression testing, automated by testing tools."},{"text":"The clinic's budget is small. Which limitation of CASE tools matters MOST in deciding how many to buy?","options":["CASE tools remove the need for analysts","CASE tools cannot draw ERDs","CASE tools always produce perfect code","Licences, hardware and training can be expensive"],"answer":3,"fb":"Cost and training are the main limitations for a small team on a small budget."},{"text":"A team member says: \"With a CASE tool we do not need careful analysis, because the tool checks everything.\" What is the BEST reply?","options":["Agreed: CASE tools replace analysis","Agreed: automatic checks find every missing requirement","The tool checks consistency, not whether the design meets the clinic's needs; a neatly drawn poor design is still poor","CASE tools only work after go-live"],"answer":2,"fb":"Automatic checks find internal errors, such as undefined fields, but cannot tell whether the system is the right one."},{"text":"The diagramming tool warns that \"NurseID\" appears in a DFD but is never defined in the data dictionary. Which benefit of CASE does this show?","options":["No need for testing","Fewer errors, through automatic checking","Lower licence costs","Faster coding"],"answer":1,"fb":"Automatic checking catches inconsistencies early, when they are cheap to fix."}],"win":"Well judged. You matched each task to a category, phase and type, explained what goes wrong without version control, and weighed CASE benefits against cost and the limits of automatic checking."}
