     "genre": "Structured response: identify, justify and discuss fact-finding tools (15 marks, practice for Paper 03)",
     "stimulus": "<p class=\"passage\">Bayside Freight operates from the Kingston Harbour cargo area. It plans to replace its paper-based cargo-tracking system. The company has five department managers and 100 clerks and drivers who use the current system. The analyst wants to know (i) each manager's goals and requirements for the new system, (ii) the answers of the clerks and drivers to 15 quantitative questions about workload and system speed, and (iii) how the current system is actually used from day to day.</p>",
     "prompt": "<p>Answer all parts.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li><b>Identify</b> the MOST appropriate fact-finding tool for each of (i), (ii) and (iii). <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li><b>Justify</b> each choice with reference to the scenario. <i>(6 marks)</i></li><li><b>Discuss</b> ONE limitation of the tool you chose for (iii) and suggest how the analyst could reduce it. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li><b>Explain</b> how review of printed material could support the investigation. <i>(3 marks)</i></li></ol>",
     "min": 220,
     "max": 420,
