     "up": {"title":"Which symbol? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"<p>In a Gane and Sarson DFD for Island Wheels Car Rentals, a trainee draws a rounded rectangle labelled \"3.0 | Rental agreements\".</p><p>What is wrong, and how should it be fixed?</p>","options":[{"t":"It should be a square, because rental agreements are external","fb":"A square is an external entity: a person or organisation. Rental agreements are data, not an entity."},{"t":"A process must be named with a verb phrase; rename it, for example \"3.0 Produce rental agreement\", or, if it is meant to hold data, redraw it as an open-ended rectangle \"D3 Rental agreements\"","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. A rounded rectangle is a process, and \"Rental agreements\" is a noun, which suits a store or flow. Fix the name or the symbol."},{"t":"Nothing is wrong: rounded rectangles may hold nouns on a level 1 DFD","fb":"Only the single process on a context diagram may be a noun, because it names the whole system."},{"t":"It should be an unlabelled arrow, because agreements move between symbols","fb":"Every data flow must be labelled. An unlabelled arrow would be a second error."}]}
