     "up": {"title":"Source, sink or both? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Harder items from Wellcare Pharmacy's prescription system. Some staff are entities, some items are hardware or data, and some are actions inside the system. Decide how each would appear on the DFD.</p>","items":[{"t":"Pharmacist: enters dispensing details and receives a daily list of prescriptions to prepare","bin":2,"fb":"Staff who supply data and receive outputs are entities, here both a source and a sink."},{"t":"Medical Council: receives a monthly report of controlled drugs dispensed","bin":1,"fb":"It only receives data from the system: a sink."},{"t":"Wholesaler: sends price lists and receives purchase orders","bin":2,"fb":"Data flows both ways: a source and a sink."},{"t":"Doctor's surgery: sends electronic prescriptions","bin":0,"fb":"It only sends data in: a source."},{"t":"The till printer that prints receipts","bin":3,"fb":"DFDs do not show hardware. The receipt is a data flow to the Patient."},{"t":"\"Check stock level\": compares prescription items with stock records","bin":3,"fb":"An action inside the system is a process, not an entity."},{"t":"The Stock file","bin":3,"fb":"Data held inside the system is a data store."},{"t":"Health Insurer: sends policy cover details when asked and receives claims","bin":2,"fb":"Data flows in both directions: source and sink."},{"t":"Customs Department: sends import clearance notices for medicines","bin":0,"fb":"It only sends data in: a source."},{"t":"A label printed for a medicine bottle","bin":3,"fb":"The label is data moving to the Patient: a data flow, not an entity."}],"win":"Well sorted. Staff who supply or receive data can be entities; hardware is never drawn; actions are processes, files are stores, and documents on the move are flows."}
