     "up": {"title":"Match the symbol to its description (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Harder: these terms describe DFD rules, errors and identifiers rather than the basic symbols. Match each term to its description.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Black hole","r":"A process with inputs but no outputs"},{"l":"Miracle","r":"A process with outputs but no inputs"},{"l":"Balancing","r":"Every external flow on the context diagram also appears on level 1"},{"l":"0","r":"The identifier of the single process on a context diagram"},{"l":"3.0","r":"The identifier of the third process on a level 1 DFD"},{"l":"D2","r":"The identifier of the second data store"},{"l":"Diagonal line in a corner","r":"Marks a duplicate copy of a symbol, drawn to avoid crossing lines"},{"l":"Noun phrase","r":"How every data flow must be labelled"}],"win":"Excellent. You know the rules a reviewer applies (no black holes or miracles, balancing, noun labels) and the identifiers that let you refer to parts of a diagram precisely."}
