     "up": {"title":"Trace the shuttle context flows (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Leeward Car Hire in Antigua takes online rental bookings. Customers send a booking request and receive a booking confirmation. The system sends a payment request to the card payment provider, which returns an authorisation code. The fleet manager sends vehicle availability and receives a daily pickup schedule. The insurance company receives a weekly list of new rentals. Sometimes a customer phones the insurance company directly to ask about cover. Match each item to how it appears on the context diagram.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"booking request","r":"From Customer to process 0"},{"l":"booking confirmation","r":"From process 0 to Customer"},{"l":"payment request","r":"From process 0 to Card Payment Provider"},{"l":"authorisation code","r":"From Card Payment Provider to process 0"},{"l":"vehicle availability","r":"From Fleet Manager to process 0"},{"l":"daily pickup schedule","r":"From process 0 to Fleet Manager"},{"l":"new rentals list","r":"From process 0 to Insurance Company"},{"l":"cover enquiry (the customer phones the insurer)","r":"Not drawn: an entity-to-entity exchange lies outside the system"}],"win":"Excellent. Every flow has a noun label and one end at process 0, the fleet manager is both a source and a sink, and the customer's phone call to the insurer is correctly left off the diagram."}
