     "up": {"title":"Name the error (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>Harder: this faulty DFD for Saba Dive Centre also contains some parts that are perfectly correct. Sort each card by its error type, or as not an error.</p>","main":"Which type of error is this, if any?","bins":["Black hole or miracle","Illegal direct connection","Labelling error","Not an error"],"items":[{"t":"D1 Bookings sends \"dive list\" straight to D2 Boats","bin":1,"fb":"Two stores connected directly."},{"t":"Diver's \"booking form\" goes straight into D1 Bookings","bin":1,"fb":"An entity connected directly to a store."},{"t":"Process 1.0 \"Record booking\" sends \"booking total\" directly to process 3.0 \"Take payment\"","bin":3,"fb":"Process-to-process flows are legal: the flow touches a process at both ends."},{"t":"Diver is drawn twice, the copy marked with a diagonal line","bin":3,"fb":"Duplicating an entity to avoid crossing lines is allowed."},{"t":"Process 2.0 \"Check equipment\" receives \"gear request\" and sends nothing anywhere","bin":0,"fb":"Inputs only: a black hole."},{"t":"D2 Boats sends \"boat capacity\" to process 1.0","bin":3,"fb":"A process reading from a store is exactly how stores are used."},{"t":"A flow from Diver to 1.0 is labelled \"book dive\"","bin":2,"fb":"A verb phrase on a flow; rename it \"booking request\"."},{"t":"Instructor sends \"medical clearance\" directly to Diver","bin":1,"fb":"Two entities connected directly: the exchange is outside the system."},{"t":"An arrow from process 3.0 to Diver has no label","bin":2,"fb":"Label omitted."},{"t":"Process 5.0 \"Send reminder\" sends \"reminder\" to Diver, but nothing flows into it","bin":0,"fb":"Outputs only: a miracle."},{"t":"Process 3.0 is labelled \"Payments\"","bin":2,"fb":"A noun on a process; rename it \"Record payment\"."}],"win":"Excellent. You classified every syllabus error and, just as importantly, recognised legal process-to-process flows, store reads and duplicated entities as correct."}
