      "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> A data flow diagram is a <b>diagram</b> (graphical representation) that shows how <b>data</b> moves into, through and out of a system.</p><p><b>(b)</b> The process is numbered 0 and named \"Car Rental System\".</p><p><b>(c)</b> The four external entities are Customer, Bank, Fleet Manager and Owner.</p><p><b>(d)</b> \"rental request\" goes from Customer to the system. \"rental agreement\" goes from the system to Customer. \"utilisation report\" goes from the system to Owner.</p><p><b>(e)</b> No data stores are shown because the stores are inside the system, hidden within the single process 0; they first appear on the level 1 DFD.</p>",
      "teacherTip": "<p>Dial-down tip: once a student completes this version, ask them to add the three remaining flows (payment request, payment confirmation, vehicle details) with directions; that bridges them to part (b) of the full question.</p>"
