      "model": "<p><b>(a)</b> A context level DFD shows the whole system as one process and no data stores, whereas a level 1 DFD shows several processes and shows the data stores.</p><p><b>(b)</b> 1.0 \"Update dive trips\", 2.0 \"Record booking\", 3.0 \"Produce dive list\".</p><p><b>(c)</b> D1 \"Dive Trips\" and D2 \"Bookings\".</p><p><b>(d)</b> (i) is a miracle. (ii) is an entity connected directly to a store. (iii) is a process labelled with a noun.</p><p><b>(e)</b> Error (ii) should be corrected by inserting process 2.0 \"Record booking\" between the Diver and the Bookings store, so the booking request goes to the process and the process writes the booking record to D2.</p>",
