     "up": {"title":"Understand, plan or carry out? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>The Carenage Water Taxi is writing an algorithm for group fares: $8 per adult, $5 per child, and 10% off the total for groups of 10 or more. For each action, choose the stage of problem solving it belongs to.</p>","items":[{"text":"The owner is asked whether a group of exactly 10 gets the discount, and the team writes down \"10 or more\" precisely.","options":["Plan the solution","Understand the problem","Carry out the plan"],"answer":1,"fb":"Pinning down the exact rule before writing steps is part of understanding the problem."},{"text":"A clerk writes: get adults; get children; total = adults × 8 + children × 5; if adults + children is 10 or more, take 10% off; display total.","options":["Plan the solution","Understand the problem","Carry out the plan"],"answer":0,"fb":"Writing the ordered steps is planning the solution: this is the algorithm."},{"text":"A crew member follows the steps for 6 adults and 4 children and charges $61.20.","options":["Carry out the plan","Understand the problem","Plan the solution"],"answer":0,"fb":"Following the steps with real data is carrying out the plan: 48 + 20 = $68, and 10 passengers earn 10% off, giving $61.20."},{"text":"Before writing any steps, the team realises it does not know whether infants travel free, and asks the owner.","options":["Carry out the plan","Understand the problem","Plan the solution"],"answer":1,"fb":"Finding a gap in what is known about the problem is part of understanding it."},{"text":"Staff move the discount step so that it comes after the total is calculated, not before.","options":["Plan the solution","Understand the problem","Carry out the plan"],"answer":0,"fb":"Putting the steps in the right order is part of planning."},{"text":"A programmer codes the agreed steps into the booking tablet, which now produces quotes at the dock.","options":["Carry out the plan","Understand the problem","Plan the solution"],"answer":0,"fb":"Coding the plan so a computer follows it is one way of carrying it out."}],"win":"Excellent. You separated understanding (clarifying rules and data), planning (ordered steps) and carrying out (following the steps, by hand or in code), and checked the arithmetic of the plan."}
