     "win": "Excellent. You can diagnose each fault and name the characteristic precisely, which is exactly what Paper 02 asks.",
     "tutor": [
      {
       "h": "Four questions",
       "p": "<p>Does it work for all cases? Does it end? Is each step precise? Is the order and next step always clear?</p>"
      },
      {
       "h": "Watch for vague words",
       "p": "<p>Words like \"right\", \"reasonable\", \"a little\" or \"high\" signal ambiguity.</p>"
      },
      {
       "h": "Dead ends and wrong order",
       "p": "<p>If a step uses something not yet calculated, or you cannot tell what to do next, the flow of control is faulty.</p>"
      }
     ],
