     "up": {"title":"Pseudocode to flowchart (Challenge)","bloom":"Apply","intro":"<p>Saba's hiking permit desk has a fuller algorithm: groups of more than 8 pay $12 per hiker per day, and smaller groups pay $15. Match each pseudocode statement to the part of the flowchart that represents it.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"START","r":"Terminal (oval) at the top"},{"l":"INPUT hikers, days","r":"Parallelogram reading data"},{"l":"IF hikers > 8 THEN","r":"Diamond with Yes and No exits"},{"l":"fee ← hikers * days * 12","r":"Rectangle on the Yes path"},{"l":"ELSE fee ← hikers * days * 15","r":"Rectangle on the No path"},{"l":"ENDIF","r":"The point where the Yes and No paths rejoin"},{"l":"OUTPUT fee","r":"Parallelogram showing a result"},{"l":"STOP","r":"Terminal (oval) at the bottom"}],"win":"Well done. Each statement has one place on the flowchart, and ENDIF has no symbol of its own: it is where the two paths of the decision meet again."}
