     "stimulus": "<p class=\"passage\">The Island Pedals Bike Rentals charges $12 per hour for each bicycle. A customer may rent several bicycles for the same number of hours. Staff need an algorithm that accepts the number of bicycles and the number of hours and displays the rental cost for any customer.</p>",
     "prompt": "<p>Answer ALL parts.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>Identify the <b>THREE</b> ways of representing an algorithm. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Write the algorithm in <b>natural language</b> as numbered steps. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Write the same algorithm in <b>pseudocode</b>. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>Describe the flowchart for this algorithm by listing, in order, each flowchart symbol you would use (name its shape) and the text inside it. <i>(3 marks)</i></li><li>The owner, who has no programming experience, wants to check the algorithm. Recommend ONE representation for her and justify your choice by comparing it with ONE other representation. <i>(3 marks)</i></li></ol><p style=\"text-align:right\"><b>[15 marks]</b></p>",
     "min": 200,
