     "up": {"title":"Which statement is processing? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","q":"<p>Sea Breeze Marina's algorithm adds up the fees for every boat that docks during a day. Which ONE of these lines is a processing statement that updates an <b>accumulator</b>?</p>","options":[{"t":"count ← count + 1","fb":"This is processing, but it adds the same amount (1) every time, so it is a counter, not an accumulator."},{"t":"OUTPUT total","fb":"This displays the total: an output statement."},{"t":"total ← total + fee","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. It adds a different value (each boat's fee) to a running total: an accumulator."},{"t":"fee ← boatLength * nights * 2.50","fb":"This is processing, but it calculates one boat's fee; it does not build a running total."}]}
