     "up": {"title":"Match the loop to its behaviour (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Harder: each card is a short loop or fragment. Match it to how it behaves.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"FOR i ← 1 TO 12","r":"Runs exactly 12 times, whatever the data"},{"l":"WHILE stock > 0 ... ENDWHILE, when stock is already 0","r":"Runs zero times"},{"l":"REPEAT INPUT pin UNTIL pin = 4821, when the correct PIN is typed first time","r":"Runs exactly once"},{"l":"INPUT score / WHILE score <> -1 ... INPUT score ... ENDWHILE","r":"A sentinel-controlled loop with a priming read"},{"l":"WHILE n < 50 DO OUTPUT n ENDWHILE","r":"An infinite loop, because nothing changes n"},{"l":"FOR n ← 20 TO 5 STEP -5","r":"Runs four times: 20, 15, 10, 5"},{"l":"REPEAT ... UNTIL x >= 10","r":"The REPEAT version of WHILE x < 10"}],"win":"Excellent. You predicted behaviour from code: fixed counts, zero passes, a single pass, the sentinel pattern, an infinite loop, a negative step and the reversed condition needed to convert WHILE to REPEAT."}
