     "up": {"title":"Complete the trace (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Dry-run this algorithm for Rainwatch Weather Club, then answer each question.</p><p>q ← 3<br>t ← 0<br>FOR i ← 1 TO 5 DO<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IF i MOD 2 = 0 THEN<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;q ← q * 2<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ELSE<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;q ← q + i<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;t ← t + q<br>ENDFOR<br>OUTPUT q, t</p>","items":[{"text":"On the first pass (i = 1), which branch runs?","options":["THEN","ELSE"],"answer":1,"fb":"1 MOD 2 = 1, so \"i MOD 2 = 0\" is FALSE and the ELSE branch runs: q becomes 3 + 1 = 4."},{"text":"What is q after the second pass (i = 2)?","options":["5","6","8"],"answer":2,"fb":"Pass 1 makes q = 4. On pass 2, 2 MOD 2 = 0 is TRUE, so q doubles to 8."},{"text":"What is t after the third pass?","options":["11","23","19"],"answer":1,"fb":"Pass 3 adds 3 to q (8 + 3 = 11). t = 4 + 8 + 11 = 23."},{"text":"What is q after the fourth pass?","options":["15","22","11"],"answer":1,"fb":"4 MOD 2 = 0, so q doubles: 11 × 2 = 22."},{"text":"What is output?","options":["22, 72","27, 45","27, 72"],"answer":2,"fb":"Pass 5 adds 5: q = 27. t = 23 + 22 + 27 = 72."},{"text":"What role does t play in this algorithm?","options":["A sentinel value","An accumulator that adds the new value of q on every pass","A counter that adds 1 on every pass"],"answer":1,"fb":"t adds a different amount (the current q) each time: an accumulator."},{"text":"If the loop were changed to FOR i ← 5 DOWNTO 1, would the output be the same?","options":["No, because the order of the passes changes the values of q","Yes, because the same values of i are used"],"answer":0,"fb":"Counting down, q becomes 8, 16, 19, 38, 39, so the output would be 39 and 120. When each pass builds on the last, order matters."}],"win":"Accurate tracing. You evaluated MOD in the condition, used the newest value of q on every pass, kept the accumulator running, and saw that reversing a loop can change the result."}
