     "up": {"title":"Find the bugs in the rainfall algorithm (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","intro":"<p>A new draft of Rainwatch Weather Club's algorithm should read the rainfall for 7 days and output the total, the average and the number of days with MORE than 10 mm. Three lines are wrong.</p>","q":"Tap EVERY line that contains an error.","lines":["1. total ← 0","2. FOR day ← 1 TO 6 DO","3.     wetDays ← 0","4.     INPUT rain","5.     total ← total + rain","6.     IF rain >= 10 THEN","7.         wetDays ← wetDays + 1","8.     ENDIF","9. ENDFOR","10. average ← total / 7","11. OUTPUT total, average, wetDays"],"correct":[1,2,5],"win":"Well found. Line 2 reads only 6 days (it should be 1 TO 7); line 3 resets the counter on every pass (move wetDays ← 0 above the loop); line 6 counts a 10 mm day, although only days with MORE than 10 mm should count (use > 10). Lines 10 and 11 are correctly placed after the loop.","miss":"Check the loop's start and end values against \"7 days\", where each counter is initialised, and whether the comparison matches \"more than 10\"."}
