     "up": {"title":"Assemble the bus fare algorithm (Challenge)","bloom":"Apply","intro":"<p>The Kingston–Spanish Town bus line now has an unknown number of passengers per trip, and the driver enters -1 after the last fare. Put the lines in order so that the algorithm outputs the total and the average fare safely.</p>","blocks":[{"t":"total ← 0 and count ← 0"},{"t":"INPUT fare (the priming read, before the loop)"},{"t":"WHILE fare <> -1 DO"},{"t":"    total ← total + fare and count ← count + 1"},{"t":"    INPUT fare (read the next fare, last line of the loop body)"},{"t":"ENDWHILE"},{"t":"IF count > 0 THEN OUTPUT total, total / count ELSE OUTPUT \"No passengers\" ENDIF"}],"win":"Correct. Initialise, prime the loop with one INPUT, update and read again inside the loop so the sentinel is never added, then output after the loop, guarding the average against a trip with no passengers."}
